  "description": "Writes an Excel workbook (.xlsx) from headings and rows with nothing but System.IO.Compression: bold frozen headings with a sort-and-filter button, fitted columns, amounts with thousands, days and moments, rows folded under the one before them, and a total row that follows the filter. Xlsx.Write(sheet, headings, rows) returns the file's bytes; Xlsx.Read(file) reads a sheet back with a cell by its heading (row[\"Litres\"]), dates from their number format and merged multi-row headings with HeadingsOn(3, 4). Zero dependencies; runs on the server and in the browser.",
